What the build does now, as rules (each one is what the product will do. Mark any that is not your policy):
  1. Refunds: if what is left to refund after earlier refunds is under 50 rupees on a normal return, nothing is paid, so 10 rupees left on a 2,000 rupee order already refunded 1,990 gives 0.
  2. Refunds: for a damaged item the earlier-refund limit includes shipping, so a 2,000 rupee order with 100 rupees shipping that already had 2,050 rupees refunded gets 50 more.
  3. Refunds: a partial return follows the same day limits, so the jacket above returned on day 10 refunds half (900 rupees) and on day 40 refunds 0.
  4. Refunds: a partial return does not refund shipping, not even when the item is damaged, so the jacket returned damaged from an order with 100 rupees shipping refunds 1,800 rupees.
  5. Refunds: if a partial return lists every item of the order, it is treated as a whole-order return, so returning jacket and kurta of the 3,000 rupee order with 10% off on day 3 refunds 2,700 rupees.
  6. Refunds: listing the same item twice in a partial return counts it once, so the jacket listed twice still refunds 1,800 rupees.
  7. Refunds: a partial return with no items listed refunds 0 rupees, while leaving the exception out means the whole order is returned.
  8. Refunds: a partial return of a final sale order gets 0 rupees unless the item is damaged, in which case the jacket refunds 1,800 rupees.
  9. Refunds: the earlier-refund limit for a partial return is checked against the whole order total, so the jacket refund of 1,800 rupees on a 2,700 rupee order already refunded 1,700 rupees is cut to 1,000 rupees.
  10. Refunds: a partial return that names an item number the order does not have makes the refund fail with an error instead of giving an amount.
  11. Refunds: an order with no items refunds 0 rupees even when reported damaged.
  12. Refunds: a discount above 100% leaves nothing to refund, so a 2,000 rupee order with a 150% discount refunds 0 rupees.
  13. Refunds: a negative discount percentage raises the refund as if the customer paid more, so a 2,000 rupee order with a -10% discount returned on day 3 refunds 2,200 rupees.
  14. Messy or missing details: days typed as text like "5", or an unreadable number, are treated as day 0, so the customer gets the full refund.
  15. Messy or missing details: an infinite number of days is treated as day 0 and gets a full refund, while a very large number like a billion days gets 0.
  16. Messy or missing details: the word damaged is recognised in any capitals and with spaces around it, so ' DAMAGED ' is treated the same as 'damaged'.
  17. Messy or missing details: the payment type is accepted in any capitals, with spaces or hyphens, so 'STORE CREDIT' and 'store-credit' are both refunded as store credit.
  18. Messy or missing details: if the payment type is blank, missing or something unknown like 'cash', the refund goes back to the card.
  19. Messy or missing details: an earlier-refund amount that is blank, negative or unreadable (such as 'abc') counts as 0 earlier refunds.
  20. Messy or missing details: an earlier-refund amount typed as text such as '500' is read as 500 rupees, and a fraction like 1,500.7 is cut to 1,500.
  21. Loyalty points: any payment other than card, such as cash or 'credit card', earns no points.
  22. Loyalty points: an order with no items, or a negative total, earns 0 points.
  23. Loyalty points: a discount of 100% or more leaves nothing to earn on, so a 1,000 rupee order with 150% off earns 0 points.
  24. Loyalty points: a negative discount percentage increases the points, so a 1,000 rupee order with -10% discount earns 22 points.
  25. Loyalty points: very large orders keep earning in the same way, so a 1 billion rupee card order earns 20,000,000 points.
  26. Messy or missing details: points are still earned when the payment type is typed with capitals or spaces, so 'Card' or ' CARD ' on a 1,000 rupee order earns 20 points.
  27. Messy or missing details: if the payment type is missing or blank, no points are earned, so a 1,000 rupee order earns 0 points.
  28. Messy or missing details: store credit written as 'store-credit' or 'Store Credit' is still recognised and earns no points.
